<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Neoptolemus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Neoptolemus, also called Pyrrhus, was in Greek mythology the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achilles">Achilles</a>, who joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trojan-war">Trojan War</a> after his father's death and killed King Priam during the sack of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/troy">Troy</a>. Legend made him the founder of the Molossian royal house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a> through his union with Andromache, and the Aeacid kings claimed descent from him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/neoptolemus.jpg" alt="Neoptolemus" width="320" height="312" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Class of Cambridge 49 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amphora_death_Priam_Louvre_F222.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
